    "editorialMarkdown": "The greedy strategy here relies on evaluating the pairwise concatenation of two items. We sort the provided text segments such that segment `x` precedes `y` if the joined string `x + y` is strictly greater than `y + x`. \n\nThe most common trap is attempting to sort the pieces purely numerically or alphabetically. For instance, comparing `3` and `30` numerically makes them seem like `30` should go first, but `303` is smaller than `330`.\n\nThe time complexity is O(n log n * L) where L is the maximum length of a string, driven by the custom sorting algorithm. Space complexity is O(n * L) to hold the array of strings.",
